# One gateway key serves the whole training fleet, so a committed credential
# file is a fleet-wide rotation mid-course, not a local reset. Every line below
# stands on its own — do not delete one without reading its reason.

# simbox-configure writes the live credentials here (files/bootstrap.sh:107)
.env
# .env.local / .env.bak, and the .env.tmp simbox-configure writes (bootstrap.sh:108)
.env.*
# any other name a maintainer picks: pizza.env, trainer.env (README:167, ps1:48)
*.env
# `docker export ... -o rootfs.tar` lands in the repo root (README "Build locally")
*.tar
# the ~900 MB release asset, rebuilt every time (build.yml:32 ASSET, README:44)
*.tar.gz
# The agent-team harness creates its working copies here, inside the repo
# root, not outside it.
.claude/worktrees/
